title LLM-Based Vulnerability Scanning Workflow

autonumber 1

participantgroup #lightblue **Interface**
    actor User
    boundary Frontend
end

participantgroup #lightgreen **Agent System**
    boundary "Agent Service" as AgentService
    control Orchestrator
    control "File Selector Agent" as FileSelector
    control "Scan Agents" as ScanAgents
    database "A2A Task Store" as Store
end

participantgroup #lightgray **Repository**
    entity Repository
end

participantgroup #lightyellow **External Entity**
    entity "Chinou Models" as Models
end

User->Frontend: Provide repository name\nand custom prompt
Frontend->AgentService: POST /a2a\nStart security scan

AgentService->Repository: Clone repository
Repository-->AgentService: Return repository file index

AgentService->Orchestrator: Send file index
Orchestrator->Store: Store initial request\nand file index
Store-->Orchestrator: Return task ID
Orchestrator-->AgentService: Return task ID
AgentService-->Frontend: Return task ID

Orchestrator->FileSelector: Select potentially\nvulnerable files
FileSelector->Models: Identify and rank vulnerable files\nMaximum 50 files
Models-->FileSelector: Return ranked file list
FileSelector-->Orchestrator: Return top 50 files
Orchestrator-->AgentService: Return selected files
AgentService-->Frontend: Stream selected files\nand file content

loop For each scan agent\nRecon, Taint, Pattern, Logic and Deep Scan
    par For each selected file\n1 to 50
        Orchestrator->ScanAgents: Analyze file using\ncustom prompt
        ScanAgents->Models: Perform vulnerability analysis
        Models-->ScanAgents: Return findings
        ScanAgents-->Orchestrator: Return scan artifacts

        Orchestrator->Store: Store phase and file artifacts
        Orchestrator-->AgentService: Return phase result
        AgentService-->Frontend: Stream result for\nphase and file
    end
end

Orchestrator->Store: Store final scan results
Orchestrator-->AgentService: Return final scan results
AgentService-->Frontend: Stream scan completion

Frontend->Frontend: Generate vulnerability summary
Frontend-->User: Display vulnerabilities
